    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **273 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city title-casing rule for owner creation.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/NormaliseCity.java`:\n- Computes a case/whitespace-insensitive key for the incoming city (reusing the existing `DuplicateKey.normalize` helper).\n- If any existing owner is already in that city (by that key), it reuses that owner's **exact** stored spelling.\n- Otherwise it title-cases the city (each word capitalised, rest lower-cased) and stores that.\n- Blank/null cities are left untouched.\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted a `normaliseCity` step (under `govern: [ transaction ]`) between `assignMembershipNumber` and `assignCustomerCode`, so the canonical city is set before the customer code (which uppercases the city) and before `save`.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests pass (`Cp12Tests` \u2014 title-casing and existing-spelling reuse), and the pre-existing `Cp10Tests` customer-code rule still holds, along with the rest of the suite.",
